Subject: [PATCH] claude: Treat unintegrated mail as revisable drafts
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: ysonztpozwrplkkvxtwsylsmnkmpksuu

The outbox was write-once: a reply or series, once pushed to
submissions, stayed as written even when a later message or a change
on trunk made it wrong. Pat then reviewed mail that its own author
already knew was out of date, and corrections could only follow as
more mail.

Until the moderator integrates it, nobody has built on a message, so
rewriting it costs nothing. process-email now checks its unintegrated
mail before each pass and revises or drops what new information has
overtaken.

The moderator may be reading a draft while it is rewritten, and may
integrate the original. A message on the list is immutable, so when a
revision conflicts with it, the list wins and anything still worth
saying goes in a new reply.
